       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error and could harm the patient.\n\n- **Order as written:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Daily maximum:** The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. This order is double that.\n- **Single-dose maximum:** The usual maximum is 800 mg per dose. 1,600 mg in one dose is well above it.\n\nAt this dose the risks include GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCommon regimens for a 70 kg adult are:\n- 400 mg PO every 6 hours (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO every 6 hours (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day), or four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nPerhaps you meant 1,600 mg total per day, such as 400 mg four times daily. Tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
