       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. You have the authority to prescribe, but I can't find any indication where 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is appropriate. It's twice the 3,200 mg/day maximum, and the dose is likely to cause serious harm, such as GI bleeding, kidney injury, or cardiovascular events. You also haven't given a rationale that would explain it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or any lower regimen you choose.\n- **Add a note to the order,** such as \"titrate per response\" or \"pharmacy to review.\"\n- **Help you get a higher dose through other channels.** If you have a rationale I'm not seeing, pharmacy or a clinical pharmacologist can review it and enter or verify the order through the proper process.\n\nIf you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than 3,200 mg/day gives, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. That could add scheduled acetaminophen, up to 1,000 mg every 8 hours, or another agent you choose.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
